From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 19 Aug 2026 07:40:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 37/37] vc4gfx: ask the kernel for the framebuffer when the
 firmware was not asked

On a Pi 3 the driver reached the silicon and then had nothing to work with:

    [VC4HVS] expecting fb: phys=0x00000000 pitch=0 1920x1080
    [VC4HVS] takeover: HDMI channel not usable (CTRL=38047880 head=0)

while the bootloader had already reported "Framebuffer @ 3e7fe000" and a
1920x1080 display.

fb_ptr is filled in by the FBALLOC batch, which only runs on a mode change. A
boot that comes up in the mode the firmware already set never asks, so the
pointer stays NULL and the HVS takeover has no plane to inherit.

On m68k-emu68 the surface is already published: Emu68 hands it over at boot and
the kernel answers KATTR_FrameBuffer, KATTR_FrameBufferPitch and their
companions -- added for the fbgfx port, and unused by this driver until now.
Reading them costs one call and closes a gap that belongs to this port rather
than to the driver.

Guarded, because elsewhere the mailbox is the right and only source.

This does not by itself make the takeover succeed: head=0 says the firmware has
not published its display list by the time a resident at priority 9 looks, and
that is the other half of the problem. It removes one of the two reasons it
cannot.
---
--- a/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/hidd/vc4gfx/vc4gfx_onbitmap.c
+++ b/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/hidd/vc4gfx/vc4gfx_onbitmap.c
@@ -11,6 +11,10 @@
 
 #include <proto/oop.h>
 #include <proto/mbox.h>
+#ifdef __EMU68__
+#include <aros/kernel.h>
+#include <proto/kernel.h>
+#endif
 #include <proto/utility.h>
 #include <assert.h>
 #include <exec/memory.h>
@@ -270,6 +274,37 @@
     D(bug("[VideoCoreGfx] %s: %d page(s) @ 0x%p, pitch %d\n",
         __PRETTY_FUNCTION__, (int)xsd->vcsd_FBPages, fb_ptr, (int)fb_pitch));
 
+#ifdef __EMU68__
+    /*
+     * Ask the kernel when the firmware has not been asked.
+     *
+     * fb_ptr is only filled in by the FBALLOC batch above, which runs on a
+     * mode change. A boot that does not change mode leaves it NULL, and the
+     * takeover then has no framebuffer to inherit -- on a Pi 3 that showed up
+     * as "expecting fb: phys=0x00000000 pitch=0" while the bootloader had
+     * reported a perfectly good surface at 0x3e7fe000.
+     *
+     * On m68k-emu68 that surface is already published: Emu68 hands it over and
+     * the kernel answers KATTR_FrameBuffer and its companions (added for the
+     * fbgfx port). Using it here costs one call and removes a gap that is
+     * ours, not the driver's.
+     */
+    if (!fb_ptr)
+    {
+        struct KernelBase *KernelBase = OpenResource("kernel.resource");
+        IPTR fb = KernelBase ? KrnGetSystemAttr(KATTR_FrameBuffer) : 0;
+
+        if (fb && fb != (IPTR)-1)
+        {
+            fb_ptr = (APTR)fb;
+            if (!fb_pitch)
+                fb_pitch = KrnGetSystemAttr(KATTR_FrameBufferPitch);
+            bug("[VideoCoreGfx] framebuffer from the kernel: 0x%p pitch %u\n",
+                fb_ptr, (unsigned)fb_pitch);
+        }
+    }
+#endif
+
     /* Phase-1 HVS bring-up: dump the firmware's live display list and PV
      * timing for this mode (read-only, self-skips on QEMU). */
     vc4_hvs_dump(xsd, (ULONG)(IPTR)fb_ptr, fb_pitch, aligned_width, height);
